{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-17T10:32:17.790Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"d0fcf7fd89442a0194ce57f7","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-web-68ig"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Reduce quadratic background force-layout cost for large browser graphs"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Round 3 of PR 216 fixes the PR-introduced main-thread blocking loop with a coalesced module worker. The pairwise repulsion algorithm itself predates the restyle and remains quadratic. A real production GraphCanvas with 2,000 synthetic item nodes and 1,999 dependency edges blocked reheat for 24,256.8 ms before the worker change. Worker runs return reheat in 0.1-0.2 ms but background completion measured 35,285.9 ms and 59,488 ms under different concurrent test loads. Final positions remain static until publication. Algorithmic scaling is a separate heavy lift from the restyle. Design sketch: benchmark seeded graph families; compare a Barnes-Hut spatial tree or bounded neighbor approximation with exact pairwise forces on small graphs; define explicit convergence, completion-time and layout-quality budgets; retain worker cancellation, control debounce and one final position publication. Evidence is in scripts/brand-browser-round3.ts and docs/brand-review.md; parent work is pm-web-i0td and the review is graph-canvas.ts:490 on PR 216."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["browser","graph","performance"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-10-17T10:32:17.790Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-17T10:32:17.790Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"codex-agent"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Record seeded 2,000-, 5,000- and 10,000-node browser measurements with graph shape, edge count, environment class, input responsiveness, completion time and layout-quality comparisons; preserve cancellation and static final publication; use behavioral regressions rather than loosening timing or coverage gates."}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"ffa61f0920244861c2cd09671e2ebc32b4938466e97adf0bdeb8dd432d634012","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"5d546dbbf81875d47e9a59df3aa80ccb3633ceeeaa4cdf9725d54ca57d60704a"}
